# HTML Project Structure

This project is an HTML project utilizing GSAP for animations and Tailwind CSS for styling. Below is the project structure:

## Directory Structure

```
.
├── src/ - Main directory containing source code
│   ├── index.html - Main page of the project
│   ├── assets/ - Contains all static assets
│   │   ├── images/ - Stores images
│   │   ├── javascripts/ - Contains JavaScript files
│   │   │   ├── gsap.min.js - GSAP library for animation
│   │   │   └── main.js - Main JavaScript file (js apply all)
│   │   └── stylesheets/ - Contains CSS files
│   │       ├── dist/ - CSS compiled by Tailwind
│   │       │   └── main.css - Compiled CSS file (never edited)
│   │       └── main.css - Main CSS file
│   └── pages/ - Contains additional HTML pages
├── tailwind.config.js - Tailwind CSS configuration
```

## Technologies Used

- **HTML**: Structures web pages
- **Tailwind CSS V3**: Utility-first CSS framework
- **GSAP**: JavaScript library for creating animations
- **JavaScript**: Handles interactivity and DOM manipulation

## Important Files

- [src/index.html](mdc:src/index.html) - Main HTML file of the project
- [tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js) - Tailwind CSS configuration
- [eslint.config.js](mdc:eslint.config.js) - ESLint configuration
- [.prettierrc](mdc:.prettierrc) - Prettier configuration
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Manages dependencies and scripts for development

## Conventions

1. Use Tailwind CSS classes in HTML; do not write new styling in [main.css](mdc:src/assets/stylesheets/main.css)
2. Always use GSAP for animations
3. Clear and semantic HTML structure
4. Modular JavaScript
